  Go parity G02/G07, P1 calling-convention storage: an AArch64 BL/RET does
  not pop eight bytes from the caller's stack. The abi-internal model must
  use extrapop=0 while retaining the existing stackshift and argument offsets.
  This is an unconditional model correction; no option is added.

  Authored source: tests/fixtures/go-aarch64-stackpop/recursive.S. Its scalar
  recursive function spills n and the first recursive result into distinct
  stack slots before the next call, implementing fib(n-1) + fib(n-2).
  The prototype fixes only the scalar input/result contract. With extrapop=8
  the first call loses its assignment and the second uses an uninitialized
  stack value instead of n. These assertions pin the complete fixed dataflow.
  The 60 bytes below are assembled with clang targeting aarch64-linux-gnu;
  they are inspected as data and never executed.
-->
